Keeps this directory in the repository so a bind-mounted `./data` already
exists and is owned by the user who cloned it. Without that, Docker creates the
mount source as root and the container's unprivileged `node` user cannot write
the SQLite database or the generated encryption key.

Everything else in here is runtime state and is git-ignored: krembonet.db and
its WAL sidecars, and encryption.key if one was generated. Back up this whole
directory — the key is not stored in the database, so a backup of the .db alone
cannot be decrypted.
